===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|en|telh₂}}
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|elatus||exalted, lofty, high}} {{suffix||ive|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|grammar}} In Semitic languages, the “adjective of superiority.” In some languages such as [[Arabic]], the concepts of [[comparative]] and [[superlative]] degree of an adjective are merged into a single form, the '''elative'''. How this form is understood or translated depends upon context and definiteness. In the absence of comparison, the elative conveys the notion of “[[greatest]]”, “[[supreme]].”
#: ''The elative of {{m|ar|كَبِير||big}} is {{m|ar|أَكْبَر||bigger/biggest, greater/greatest}}.''

